{
  "description": "Hand-specified golden cases for the published catalogue tools, written from the contract text alone and never generated from an implementation. Unit 1b freezes the get_model exact-ID and marker-lookup cases against lookup.json (oracle case 1 scenario); later units append their own cases to 'cases'. The envelope-freeze correction froze the successful PURE get_model payload: the top-level field set (including provider_staleness), the endpoint field set and the counts cardinalities (exact_matches, endpoints, distinct_raw_ids, marker_group_labels) are final. Counts describe the returned lookup result only. The shared-ID correction gives the two providers tracking vendor/shared intentionally conflicting, valid per-provider metadata (synthetic-a: large text-only context; synthetic-b: image input with a smaller context) so that metadata attachment by (provider, raw model_id) is testable; every snapshot_id was recomputed from the lookup.json fixture body. Unit 1c-a appends four metadata edge-case goldens against metadata-edge-cases.json (unknown-context / known-context / zero-context / unknown-description, plus a stale zero-ID second provider), each with a complete literal payload whose snapshot_id is the real canonical hash of that fixture body. Unit 1c-b1 appends two capability goldens against capability-unknown.json (an all-null-capability model and a known-empty-lists model, plus a stale zero-ID second provider); the two ids are not free-marker variants, so each query returns exactly one endpoint, all four counts are 1, and both payloads preserve the null-versus-empty distinction.",
